# A movie's card behind another app, and back (cavekit-flash.md R10, T-580). Behind Notes the daemon publishes no
# frame of it (the card is frozen) and gives back the governor's boost the player took (engine patch 0119: when every
# card of the daemon is behind); the player itself runs on, as the stock browser's does (its sound: flash-sound-
# background). Back from the card view, the movie draws and takes a tap within 2 s, and the boost is taken again.
# The instrumented movie plays a Sorenson clip, so its region changes frame to frame (alone it draws one still frame,
# and a rate could not be read from it: round 2026-11-18), 120 s long so it still plays when the card is back (the 20 s
# clip had ended by then: round finger-2026-11-17).
id: flash-background-card
section: Flash
item: A movie's card behind another app publishes no frames and gives back the CPU boost within 5 s; back in front the movie draws and takes a tap within 2 s
shells: enyo mochi mojo
page: http://192.168.1.245:8077/jihad-flash-instr.html?movie=avm2&vars=video=http://192.168.1.245:8097/video/gen-spark-240-120s.flv
kit: cavekit-flash.md R10
wait rect 'sel:embed' 30
expect flash-rate m 3 5 100
card-away com.palm.app.notes
wait line 'cpu boost release (every card' 5
mark
wait quiet 'painted shmid' 4
card-back
wait changed m 2
expect flash-rate m 2 5 100
wait line 'cpu boost acquire (a card in front' 3
flash-tap m 400 300 showAll 100 100
wait text down "down " 2
